From 32d2aef3ae9ff74fc9ffef1cb65daf2e0e876860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:33:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] profile: recover the counts of computed goto edges

This is an alternative to
https://gcc.gnu.org/pipermail/gcc-patches/2026-August/728947.html, which
answered Honza's comments at
https://gcc.gnu.org/pipermail/gcc-patches/2026-August/728898.html, respun to
address the Sashiko review on the previous version.  That
patch gives each target of a computed goto an even, guessed share of the
remaining probability.  This patch recovers the measured count of each
target instead.  This is better: the targets keep their measured
distribution, so bb-reorder knows the likely target, which was a point of
the review.  The entry count and the consistency of the profile also
become correct, and 728947 does not fix these.  Ignored edges that are
not computed goto edges, for example those of setjmp receivers, keep
their current probabilities.

branch_prob cannot instrument abnormal edges.  It replaces each of them by
two fake edges, from the entry block to the destination and from the
source to the exit block.  It ignores the abnormal edge.  The ignored edge
keeps a zero count.  So compute_branch_probabilities gives every edge of a
factored computed goto a precise never probability, although the blocks
it reaches have measured counts.

Since r16-4164, rebuild_frequencies calls determine_unlikely_bbs for
read profiles.  Its forward propagation cannot pass the dispatch, so it
sets the count of the whole dispatch loop to zero.  When ceval.c of
CPython 3.14.5 is compiled with its training profile, 2851 of the 2899
blocks of _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault end up as never executed.  The fake
flow also inflates the entry count, so the node count of that function
counts its dispatches as calls.

When the only abnormal edge into a block comes from a computed goto, the
fake edge from the entry block carries exactly its flow.  Move the flow
back to the abnormal edge.  Remove it from the fake edge of the computed
goto and from the entry and exit counts.  The profile stays
flow-consistent, the dispatch keeps its measured targets and the entry
count becomes the number of calls again.  In the same compilation, 645
of the 2908 blocks of _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault keep a zero count, the
code that the training run did not execute.

In gcc.dg/tree-prof/comp-goto-2.c, run is called 10 times and dispatches
20020 times.  The edges from its dispatch change as follows, and the node
count of run changes from 20030 to 10:

  target    before              after
  op_inc    [never] count:0     [0.0%] count:10
  op_dec    [never] count:0     [50.0%] count:10000
  op_jnz    [never] count:0     [50.0%] count:10000
  op_halt   [never] count:0     [0.0%] count:10

On CPython 3.14.5 built with PGO and LTO on aarch64 (Neoverse V2), this
patch reduces the geometric mean run time of 17 pyperformance benchmarks
by 8.9% compared to trunk.  In the python binary,
_PyEval_EvalFrameDefault has 80% fewer stack accesses and 10% fewer
instructions.

Bootstrapped and regression tested on aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu and
x86_64-pc-linux-gnu.

Ok for trunk?
Thanks,
Kyrill

Cc: Jan Hubicka <hubicka@ucw.cz>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* profile.cc (compute_branch_probabilities): Move the flow of the
	fake edges of a computed goto back to its abnormal edges.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/tree-prof/comp-goto-2.c: New test.
	* gcc.dg/tree-prof/comp-goto-3.c: New test.

Signed-off-by: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>
---
 gcc/profile.cc | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/profile.cc b/gcc/profile.cc
index 17841fc723a..933c5458cca 100644
--- a/gcc/profile.cc
+++ b/gcc/profile.cc
@@ -666,6 +666,62 @@ compute_branch_probabilities (unsigned cfg_checksum, unsigned lineno_checksum)
        error ("corrupted profile info: profile data is not flow-consistent");
    }
 
+  /* branch_prob replaced each abnormal edge by fake edges from the entry
+     block to its destination and from its source to the exit block.  When
+     the only abnormal predecessor of a block is a computed goto, the fake
+     edge from the entry block carries exactly the flow of that edge.  Move
+     it back to the edge so that the dispatch keeps its measured targets.  */
+  if (!inconsistent || flag_profile_correction)
+    {
+      for (edge fake : ENTRY_BLOCK_PTR_FOR_FN (cfun)->succs)
+	{
+	  if (!(fake->flags & EDGE_FAKE) || EDGE_INFO (fake)->ignore)
+	    continue;
+
+	  edge abnormal = NULL;
+	  unsigned num_ignored = 0;
+	  for (edge e : fake->dest->preds)
+	    if (EDGE_INFO (e)->ignore)
+	      {
+		abnormal = e;
+		num_ignored++;
+	      }
+	  if (num_ignored != 1)
+	    continue;
+	  gimple *last = last_nondebug_stmt (abnormal->src);
+	  if (!last || !computed_goto_p (last))
+	    continue;
+
+	  /* The fake edge from the computed goto to the exit block carries the
+	     flow, unless the block also has a fake edge from the entry block
+	     and that one took the place of it on the spanning tree.  */
+	  edge out = find_edge (abnormal->src, EXIT_BLOCK_PTR_FOR_FN (cfun));
+	  if (!out || EDGE_INFO (out)->ignore)
+	    continue;
+	  /* Counters of a program with threads need not be consistent, so do
+	     not move more than the computed goto has left.  */
+	  gcov_type flow = MIN (edge_gcov_count (fake), edge_gcov_count (out));
+	  if (flow <= 0)
+	    continue;
+
+	  edge_gcov_count (abnormal) = flow;
+	  edge_gcov_count (fake) -= flow;
+	  edge_gcov_count (out) -= flow;
+	  bb_gcov_count (ENTRY_BLOCK_PTR_FOR_FN (cfun)) -= flow;
+	  bb_gcov_count (EXIT_BLOCK_PTR_FOR_FN (cfun)) -= flow;
+	  /* An emptied fake edge was not measured to be dead, so keep it from
+	     turning a partial profile into a guess below.  */
+	  if (!edge_gcov_count (fake))
+	    fake->probability = profile_probability::never ();
+	  if (!edge_gcov_count (out))
+	    out->probability = profile_probability::never ();
+	  if (dump_file)
+	    fprintf (dump_file, "Computed goto edge from %i to %i, count: %"
+		     PRId64 "\n", abnormal->src->index, abnormal->dest->index,
+		     (int64_t) flow);
+	}
+    }
+
   /* For every edge, calculate its branch probability and add a reg_note
      to the branch insn to indicate this.  */
 
-- 
2.56.1

